Respect the dialogModal setting in eventClick().

When "Open event title link target in a modal popup" is enabled, eventDidMount()
adds Drupal's use-ajax and data-dialog-type attributes to the event anchor, so
core's dialog system already handles the click. eventClick() then runs as well
and unconditionally navigates -- window.open() when openEntityInNewTab is set,
otherwise location.href -- which races the AJAX dialog. In practice the dialog
opens and the browser immediately leaves the page, so the modal option cannot be
used at all.

preventDefault() does not help: it stops the anchor's default navigation, not
the explicit window.open()/location.href calls further down.

This adds an early return so eventClick() defers to the dialog system when
dialogModal is on, matching the behaviour the setting advertises.

Filed against fullcalendar_view 5.2.5.

--- a/js/fullcalendar_view.js
+++ b/js/fullcalendar_view.js
@@ -195,6 +195,13 @@
       Drupal.ajax.bindAjaxLinks(document.body);
 
       return false;
     }
+    // When the event link is configured to open in a modal, Drupal's dialog
+    // system handles this click through the use-ajax attributes added in
+    // eventDidMount(). Navigating here as well would race that AJAX request.
+    if (viewSettings.dialogModal) {
+      return false;
+    }
+
     // Open a new window to show the details of the event.
     if (thisEvent.url) {
       let eventURL = new URL(thisEvent.url, location.origin);
